source=&lt;owner_resource&gt;</code> <br><br> <code>GET /metafields?owner_resource=subscription&amp;owner_id=&lt;subscription_id&gt;</code> <br><br> <code>GET /metafields?owner_resource=customer&amp;owner_id=&lt;customer_id&gt;</code> <br><br> <code>GET /metafields?owner_resource=store&amp;owner_id=&lt;store_id&gt;</code> <br><br> <strong>When getting metafields, you must specify owner_resource in the URL. It can be <code>address</code>, <code>store</code>, <code>customer</code>, <code>subscription</code>, <code>order</code>, <code>charge</code></strong> <br><br> You can list metafields that are created for all subscription objects using: <br><br>  <code>GET /metafields?owner_resource=subscription</code> - <code>**owner_id**</code> in the response will be the ID of the subscription.</p>
</div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div class="mt-8" data-v-7f693ec6><span class="text-sm text-mainText" data-v-7f693ec6>Scopes:</span> <span class="inline-block border border-white shadow-keyline text-sm text-mainText rounded-md px-1 py-0.5 mb-1 mr-1 lowercase font-mono font-extralight scope" data-v-7f693ec6>
